<title>HUNGARY: Hungary net foreign debt drops to $12.22bln in Apr.</title>
<headline>Hungary net foreign debt drops to $12.22bln in Apr.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-07-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hungary's net foreign debt dropped to $12,215.1 million in April from $12,570.3 million in March, according to the preliminary figures released by the National Bank of Hungary on Tuesday.</p>
<p>    FIGURES IN $MILLION     April 97    March 97    April 96</p>
<p>    Net foreign debt	  12,215.1    12,570.3    14,819.5</p>
<p>International reserves and</p>
<p>	other foreign assets  11,687.3    12,347.3    13,012.6</p>
<p>    International reserves   7,904.5     8,510.9     9,685.2</p>
<p>    - Gold			    34.3	  35.1	  41.7</p>
<p>    Gross foreign debt	23,428.6    24,442.5    27,832.1</p>
<p>Net foreign debt of</p>
<p>	government and NBH     7,385.4     7,570.1    10,284.4</p>
<p>Gross foreign debt of</p>
<p>	government and NBH    16,032.3    16,852.9    20,481.6</p>
<p>NOTE - Debt figures exclude inter-company loans. The NBH values gold at London market prices.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom (36 1)0327 4040</p>
</text>
